  "main_theorem": "JSP422FiniteHead.unrestricted_once_exists_rearrangement",
  "scope": "For nonnegative real lengths tending to zero with divergent sum, once coverage in the pinned open-ball unit-circle model has probability one iff some length is at least one or the Shepp condition holds for a decreasing rearrangement. The existential theorem obtains that rearrangement from the original source; the finite-prefix bridge needs 0<=a_n<1 only in the removed prefix.",
  "scope_boundary": "This adds the missing once-versus-tail bridge and the >=1 endpoint branch in the pinned open-ball model. Shepp 1972 assumes strictly subunit lengths; the endpoint statement is explicitly an extension to the abbreviated original-problem webpage model, not an assertion about unspecified endpoint conventions in the paper.",
  "axiom_whitelist": [
    "propext",
    "Classical.choice",
    "Quot.sound"
  ],
  "attribution": "The unchanged upstream formalization credits L. A. Shepp for the mathematics and Codex / GPT-5.6 Sol for formalization. The three included bridge files add the finite-prefix probability argument and the explicit open-arc endpoint assembly. No first-proof, priority, recipient or award-eligibility claim.",
  "source_distribution": "The four upstream modules are referenced by immutable URLs and hashes, not included. Only three new bridges and their audit harness are included.",
  "execution_policy": "A public replay freshly compiles all seven custom modules, then the 17-declaration audit and four target checkers in a fresh isolated output directory. It never reuses private olean artifacts or writes the supplied Mathlib cache."
